{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources","id":921583,"title":"Job, Paygrade and Resources.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-26T11:28:03-07:00","id":921583,"title":"Job, Paygrade and Resources.","content":"Wanted to ask this since just got an application on rpol, <br /> <br /> A lawyer with Resources 2, and was like &quot;What the heck?&quot; <br /> <br /> Player had an explanation that made a... fair degree of sense in context.<br /> <br /> but wanted to ask.. what resources should someone be able to achieve in a certain career.<br /> <br /> obviously their may be some freak exceptions.<br /> <br /> Like a hereditary Millionaire who works for the FBI, or the cook for a REALLY REALLY classy restaraunt.<br /> <br /> Heres my attempt at a list.<br /> <br /> SSI Reciptent: None, just enough to scrape by.<br /> <br /> Laborer: 1, 2 for supervisors.<br /> <br /> Novelist 1-5 many novelist, barely get by, but some do manage to write storys like harry potter, so phenominal that they become multi millionaires.<br /> <br /> Criminals: <br /> <br /> PickPockets, and thugs, might have Resources 1, or what their dayjob provides, <br /> <br /> Hitmen, will have Resources 3, or maybe 4 for the very best.<br /> <br /> School Teacher<br /> <br /> Resources 2, or maybe 3 (Have a mom whos a school teacher she whines all the time about how underpaid she is)<br /> <br /> Lawyer<br /> <br /> On average should be 3-4<br /> <br /> Though the very best, get enough to retire young, at Resources 5 ,thanks to &quot;Trials of the Century&quot; Like OJ simpson , and the OKC bombing trial.<br /> <br /> Medicine<br /> <br /> Nurses and interns have 1-2 Doctors rarely have under 4<br /> <br /> Police Generally have Resources 2, Captains or those with distinguished records have 3 and the chief of police, or FBI has a 4<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything I missed or you think I gave too much or too little?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:33:55-07:00","id":921625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources#post921583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heres my attempt at a list.<br /> <br /> SSI Reciptent: None, just enough to scrape by.<br /> <br /> Laborer: 1, 2 for supervisors.<br /> <br /> Novelist 1-5 many novelist, barely get by, but some do manage to write storys like harry potter, so phenominal that they become multi millionaires.<br /> <br /> Criminals:<br /> <br /> PickPockets, and thugs, might have Resources 1, or what their dayjob provides,<br /> <br /> Hitmen, will have Resources 3, or maybe 4 for the very best.<br /> <br /> School Teacher<br /> <br /> Resources 2, or maybe 3 (Have a mom whos a school teacher she whines all the time about how underpaid she is)<br /> <br /> Lawyer<br /> <br /> On average should be 3-4<br /> <br /> Though the very best, get enough to retire young, at Resources 5 ,thanks to &quot;Trials of the Century&quot; Like OJ simpson , and the OKC bombing trial.<br /> <br /> Medicine<br /> <br /> Nurses and interns have 1-2 Doctors rarely have under 4<br /> <br /> Police Generally have Resources 2, Captains or those with distinguished records have 3 and the chief of police, or FBI has a 4<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything I missed or you think I gave too much or too little?</div> </div> </div> </div>Decent enough list. However,<br /> SSI recievers can be higher if they had saved quite a bit. <br /> Laborers, it depends. A good architect, can be a 3 resources.. while a concreter is practically always gonna get work..<br /> Teachers, it depends if Elementary through high level, OR college/uni, and whether tenured or not..<br /> Lawyer is also dependent. A divorce lawyer might not be rich, but is always gonna get work. Where as a tax attourney/defense lawyer might get a lot more, but only have sporadic clients.<br /> Same with a personal injury lawyer..<br /> <br /> On the Docs, it also depends on field. Neuro surgeon, damn skippy he's gonna be high. Foot doc, maybe a steady 2-3..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:34:44-07:00","id":921663,"title":"","content":"Am on SSI myself, were not allowed to save more then $2,000 up.<br /> <br /> My neurologist, is well dressed, but not ridiculously so. a nuro surgeon will be even higher then a neurologist I take it? (She diagnosed and treats my MS) <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:45:48-07:00","id":921669,"title":"","content":"It also depends a bit on if you're using the pre-V20 version where Resource ratings are more defined, or the V20 version that's much more vague.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't actually put most doctors over 3 with the V20 version. Becoming a doctor often involves accruing a large amount of debt that results in their high wages not translating into the sorts of assets that Resources 4-5 assumes.<br /> <br /> Though this is also something that applies across professions. How you handle your money matters. I know people with six figure salaries that basically live at Resources 2 because they've horribly mismanaged their finances over the years, and others that make significantly less but would fall under the Resources 3 description by being very smart with their money.<br /> <br /> Age matters as well, simply because even in professions that are considered well paying, younger members of the profession generally get paid less (not just because they're starting, but because there are biases regarding age and promotions/raises*). As well, younger members of the profession are more likely to be in significant debt via education and/or have not had time to start building non-liquid assets.<br /> <br /> Then there's who you work for. Lawyers are a great example beyond what garhkal pointed out. An assistant district attorney, a public defender, and a defense lawyer for a major law firm, are all looking at wildly different pay rates everything else being equal. The DA's office is generally far better funded (and thus better paying) than the PD office, but in both you get stuck with the cases you get, while a private firm can select their cases and demand higher pay.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> * - As an example, my uncle went back to school and got his DO over an MD, when he was 35. Between opting to go DO, and his age, by the time he was 45, he was making money similar to other doctors in the same age category, not other doctors that had been practicing for less than 10 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-26-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:17:07-07:00","id":922020,"title":"","content":"I don't think a lawyer needs a high resources level. It's the field I'm going into, and the pay I can expect for my first couple of years as a criminal defence barrister is barely above the poverty line. Now, that's specific to Australia, but the general pattern holds up in most legal markets, with the first few years for a lot of lawyers being pretty lean when it comes to pay and benefits, or pay compared to hours worked. Even after that, it's only 'good' (let's say 2, 2.5), not 'great' (3+), until you get some good years or make your name for particularly good work. Now add in that the job market for lawyers is shrinking while an enormous number of hungry young lawyers come out of the law schools with significant debts they need to pay off and a willingness to work for less than their established counterparts, the cut throat competition for positions in the high-paying firms, and that a lot of work either doesn't pay or pays a pittance (looking at you, public defense work and pro-bono work!) and you have a recipe for lawyers who's <i>functional</i> wealth is only Resources 1, and who's dreaming of when he can fill in that metaphorical second dot.<br /> <br /> Lawyers can easily rise from 1 to 5+ over their lifetime, but for a lot of them, they'll never get above 3. It's helpful to keep in mind that in Revised and V20 both, 1 dot encompasses anyone below the financial middle class who isn't functionally destitute (so, most of the working class, but not all), 2-3 cover the middle classes, and 4+ is a rich bugger/capitalist parasite on the working man/hero of the almighty dollar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:14:44-07:00","id":922101,"title":"","content":"And many lawyers who DO make the big bucks also spend 60+ hours in the office!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:39:18-07:00","id":922193,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that skilled blue collar work can pull in more money than a lot of white collar office work does, so a contractor or factory worker isn't necessarily going to be &quot;lower class&quot; even if he dropped out of high school to learn a trade. Likewise, skilled RNs can earn low six figures, while the costs of running a practice and paying insurance can drop a doctor's effective income into mid- to high-five figure brackets despite pretty high hourly rates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:58:23-07:00","id":922205,"title":"","content":"In regards to school teacher, it varies from school to school, private vs public, state to state, country to country, etc; also many schools have systems where additional qualifications increase your pay grade (examples masters, doctorate, certifications) so I would label it as Resources 1-3 to represent the variance in region and qualifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:03:45-07:00","id":922207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=922193#post922193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that skilled blue collar work can pull in more money than a lot of white collar office work does, so a contractor or factory worker isn't necessarily going to be &quot;lower class&quot; even if he dropped out of high school to learn a trade. Likewise, skilled RNs can earn low six figures, while the costs of running a practice and paying insurance can drop a doctor's effective income into mid- to high-five figure brackets despite pretty high hourly rates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be sure were on the same page you mean malpractice insurance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:42:50-07:00","id":922225,"title":"","content":"Probably not just malpractice. A doctor that's running their own private practice, or is a partner in one, is responsible for not only their personal malpractice insurance, but a host of other forms of insurance pretty much every small business owner has to deal with as well (at least in some form or another).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T15:22:03-07:00","id":922246,"title":"","content":"on Lawyer did I seem too cynical about &quot;Trials of the century?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T15:50:55-07:00","id":922254,"title":"","content":"As Heavy Arms says, not just malpractice insurance but also things like health and unemployment insurance for the staff, renter's or owner's insurance for the physical location, that sort of thing. I would think that as a doctor running a practice one would have to pay all the overhead of running the business before getting around to one's own salary, so that could take a hit if there are a few unexpected lean months in a row.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T21:15:18-07:00","id":922441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=922246#post922246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on Lawyer did I seem too cynical about &quot;Trials of the century?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, but most of those cases aren't that common and surprisingly, they often don't pay the millions of dollars claimed in terms of 'real pay' because the costs are often through the roof as well. The lawyer's payment for a long, high profile case might seem high, but it goes to a team of lawyers, paralegals, expert witnesses, lost opportunity costs from missed work, travel costs, rental costs, filing fees, etcetera.<br /> <br /> The best pay doesn't come, typically, from the high profile cases unless the client is filthy rich. It comes from working for the large, high-flying corporate law firms and reaching partnership level. This is also the hardest slog a lawyer faces - it's not uncommon to work 60+ hours a week, as Garkhal says, as a <i>senior</i> associate at those places, and when you're a junior, all bets are off and you better not plan on doing anything but eating, breathing, sleeping, and shitting company business on a salary that's really only adequate for someone working 40 hours a week. It's the trade-off - you work hard and suffer until you hit relatively easy street, but even then, you're probably still working a surprising number of hours for a person of your wealth.<br /> <br /> Most lawyers also don't retire after getting a high profile case. That's the worst career move - if you win a high profile case, or put up a damned good case that loses because it was unwinnable rather than because you're incompetent, you're going to want to keep practicing because clients will flock and doors will open. Stephen Jones, the lawyer who lead McVeigh's defence team, is still in practice today to use one of your examples. On the OJ example, Cochran, Shapiro, Dershowitz, and several others all remained in practice for years or still practice. Law is not a field that encourages young retirement - as you age and grow in experience, demand grows for you, and with it the opportunities to make good money grow. It only slackens if you start to lose or lose your faculties, or if factors unforeseen (e.g. your entire field of specialty is no longer needed (looking at you, marijuana specialists!) because it's no longer a crime.) rise to complicate affairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T23:10:23-07:00","id":922475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=922254#post922254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Heavy Arms says, not just malpractice insurance but also things like health and unemployment insurance for the staff, renter's or owner's insurance for the physical location, that sort of thing. I would think that as a doctor running a practice one would have to pay all the overhead of running the business before getting around to one's own salary, so that could take a hit if there are a few unexpected lean months in a row.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. Heck its not even the docs themselves who just have malpractice insurance to worry about. Take for example one of my fellow Electronics technicians that got out after 8 years on my first Carrier.. He had a # of NEC (naval enlisted classification) codes dealing with 2m and calibration, including medical gear calibration and repair..<br /> He got out and went right to work for a hospital over in Richmond Va, at 85k for the FIRST 2 years, which was to get bumped up to 120 in the 3-6 year block.. BUT out of that, he had 25k a year for HIS malpractice insurance payments..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T23:52:55-07:00","id":922484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources#post921583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Novelist 1-5 many novelist, barely get by, but some do manage to write storys like harry potter, so phenominal that they become multi millionaires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, to live in that sweet world.<br /> <br /> Most novelists - any artistic profession, really - only &quot;get by&quot; because they have a day job to supplement their work. Stephen King isn't rich because he put out a few books; he's written 60 books and 200 short stories. J.K. Rowling isn't rich just because she wrote Harry Potter - she was unemployed, divorced, and living on the dole while writing the first book - she's rich because of licensing and merchandising.<br /> <br /> And what some people seem to miss, writing is a <i>job</i>, and it's hard. It's not &quot;you have to be somewhere and punch a clock, manual labor style&quot; hard, but rather &quot;you need to have <i>x</i> amount of pages turned in by <i>y</i> date or we'll find someone else&quot; hard. Sure, you get to stay home in your pajamas while you work, but it's hard to get motivated sometimes, it's hard to stay focused with all the distractions being home provides, it's hard to receive what seems like nothing but negative feedback on the awesome things you wrote, and sometimes you find yourself still working at 4:30 in the morning...<br /> <br /> Sorry, got a little off track there.<br /> <br /> Being an artistic professional requires an amount of self-discipline most supernaturals, quite simply, don't have time for. Going back to King, he writes a minimum of 6 pages a day, and each page can take anywhere from 10 minutes to an hour. And that's just the act of <i>writing</i> - that doesn't even include revisions, plotting, pacing, research, even something as basic as conceiving a story. That's literally just hours in front of a computer, typing.<br /> <br /> And unless you're Pynchon, you don't get high Resources without having to make public appearances, glad-hand, give interviews - basically, doing a ton of press, promotion, and publicity.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> (An anecdote: In the late 90s, I was casual acquaintances with members of the band Skrew, who were working on their third album. The band members all worked full time at a coffee shop in Austin to support themselves. They would work all day and then spend several hours recording and practicing. Then they did it all over again the next day, and that's all they did. There was no time left over to fight the Wyrm, or the Sabbat, or whoever. But they were doing what they loved.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T06:40:07-07:00","id":922579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=922441#post922441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, but most of those cases aren't that common and surprisingly, they often don't pay the millions of dollars claimed in terms of 'real pay' because the costs are often through the roof as well. The lawyer's payment for a long, high profile case might seem high, but it goes to a team of lawyers, paralegals, expert witnesses, lost opportunity costs from missed work, travel costs, rental costs, filing fees, etcetera.<br /> <br /> The best pay doesn't come, typically, from the high profile cases unless the client is filthy rich. It comes from working for the large, high-flying corporate law firms and reaching partnership level. This is also the hardest slog a lawyer faces - it's not uncommon to work 60+ hours a week, as Garkhal says, as a <i>senior</i> associate at those places, and when you're a junior, all bets are off and you better not plan on doing anything but eating, breathing, sleeping, and shitting company business on a salary that's really only adequate for someone working 40 hours a week. It's the trade-off - you work hard and suffer until you hit relatively easy street, but even then, you're probably still working a surprising number of hours for a person of your wealth.<br /> <br /> Most lawyers also don't retire after getting a high profile case. That's the worst career move - if you win a high profile case, or put up a damned good case that loses because it was unwinnable rather than because you're incompetent, you're going to want to keep practicing because clients will flock and doors will open. Stephen Jones, the lawyer who lead McVeigh's defence team, is still in practice today to use one of your examples. On the OJ example, Cochran, Shapiro, Dershowitz, and several others all remained in practice for years or still practice. Law is not a field that encourages young retirement - as you age and grow in experience, demand grows for you, and with it the opportunities to make good money grow. It only slackens if you start to lose or lose your faculties, or if factors unforeseen (e.g. your entire field of specialty is no longer needed (looking at you, marijuana specialists!) because it's no longer a crime.) rise to complicate affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good points.<br /> <br /> Remember on the Dare Devil Movie<br /> <br /> &quot;What does &quot;good&quot; mean?&quot; (In reference to clients) <br /> <br /> &quot;Good means rich and guilty&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmmmn on lawyer, would it be too difficult for Vampires or Garou to work in law?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T08:40:37-07:00","id":922652,"title":"","content":"It depends on a lot of factors.<br /> <br /> Though neither is really viable as a trial lawyer (vampires - too much stuff that needs done during the day - and Garou have the Curse). There's still plenty of kinds of lawyers out there who rarely actually have to deal with people outside of their firm/company.<br /> <br /> Vampires are, in general, going to run into the &quot;hey, this guy doesn't age&quot; issue since lawyers inherently have to deal with other people. A vampire that wants to stay involved in the law would probably be best served by using Ghoul proxies that rely on the vampire's mundane and supernatural skills to advance their cases.<br /> <br /> Garou struggle with a different problem; but a similar conclusion. Garou old enough (Rank and Gifts) to make interacting with humans more viable, and a young law student/fresh lawyer are looking at trying to balance to very time intensive efforts. Assuming a Garou manage to balance their duties with the difficulty of getting a degree in the first place, they're stuck in the same situation as vampires. They'd do their best helping kinfolk lawyers rather than being the face of their firm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:01:29-07:00","id":922670,"title":"","content":"oh curious what kinds of rolls would come up in a Court case? <br /> <br /> especialy a garou or kinfolk lawyer, against some Pentex Bigshot lawyer saying &quot;We want this tract of land under iminent domain, think of all the jobs we'd be able to create!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:06:09-07:00","id":922735,"title":"","content":"The kind of rolls would vary a lot; but they don't all have to fall on the same person (hence bigger trials tend to have teams of lawyers on top of the standard support staff). You need Intelligence and Wits for the legal maneuvering that goes into establishing the facts, evidence, spotting technicalities, etc. Politics and Bureaucracy can deal with some of of the outside-of-the-court-room dealings that might need to happen. In a jury trial, you need at least one lawyer that has the social stats to influence the jury; there's plenty of different approaches that could be used like any other social roll.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the support staff, you've got some number of paralegals doing a lot of the grunt work on the law side of things, and any bigger firm has their own private investigator (or more) around in case they want to dig into things.<br /> <br /> As a side note, Pentex can't claim eminent domain. Eminent domain is a power of the state. Pentex would have to get a government official of the appropriate level (varies) to lead the effort (which isn't necessarily hard, but it isn't a hill even very corrupt politicians want to die on if there's any significant public resistance).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:21:00-07:00","id":922746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=922484#post922484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being an artistic professional requires an amount of self-discipline most supernaturals, quite simply, don't have time for. Going back to King, he writes a minimum of 6 pages a day, and each page can take anywhere from 10 minutes to an hour. And that's just the act of <i>writing</i> - that doesn't even include revisions, plotting, pacing, research, even something as basic as conceiving a story. That's literally just hours in front of a computer, typing.<br /> <br /> And unless you're Pynchon, you don't get high Resources without having to make public appearances, glad-hand, give interviews - basically, doing a ton of press, promotion, and publicity.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call on the public appearances and such. So it could be real hard for a vampiric artists to make it big.. Kinfolk, or ghouls would have the easier time however..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=922652#post922652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou struggle with a different problem; but a similar conclusion. Garou old enough (Rank and Gifts) to make interacting with humans more viable, and a young law student/fresh lawyer are looking at trying to balance to very time intensive efforts. Assuming a Garou manage to balance their duties with the difficulty of getting a degree in the first place, they're stuck in the same situation as vampires. They'd do their best helping kinfolk lawyers rather than being the face of their firm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck i could also see issues with Frenzies cause of how hectic and stressful trials can get..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=922670#post922670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious what kinds of rolls would come up in a Court case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Int+ law, Per or Cha+public speaking, Cha+intimidation vs willpower...<br /> <br /> Just some i can think of.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T14:24:16-07:00","id":923483,"title":"","content":"I think vampire musicians and theatre actors would have the easiest time of it in the Arts, as the bulk of work out there is at night. (And if they have Presence, easy-to-use vampiric abilities could directly influence audience response. If they're writing, sculpting, or painting, financial success would depend on the responses of either large numbers of people or small numbers of <i>just the right people</i> that they might never have direct contact with. They'd need to be both very good and very lucky.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T16:59:23-07:00","id":923573,"title":"","content":"oh a &quot;Career&quot; I forgot, &quot;Daytrading&quot; that tends to yield either nothing, or Resources 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T17:06:31-07:00","id":923576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=923483#post923483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think vampire musicians and theatre actors would have the easiest time of it in the Arts, as the bulk of work out there is at night. (And if they have Presence, easy-to-use vampiric abilities could directly influence audience response. If they're writing, sculpting, or painting, financial success would depend on the responses of either large numbers of people or small numbers of <i>just the right people</i> that they might never have direct contact with. They'd need to be both very good and very lucky.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is that tricky issue with getting suddenly very famous and the masquerade.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"