imate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going by V20 Resources, which are better than previous edition resources because they do not have to be adjusted for inflation. And yes, enlisted (E1-E6) are relatively poor. While you can game the system somewhat by sleeping on base and eating at the mess hall, it is not possible to support a family on one enlisted salary (two E4 could do it because of various allowances, but you risk having both parents being deployed). An E1, for example, makes the equivalent of federal minimum wage while an E6 could make more money as a manager at McDonalds. People make sacrifices when they enlist in the US military.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> in that case what's the incentive to become a soldier? when you could make about just as much from a blue collar job with no skill requirements? why risk your life?<br /> <br /> concerning pentex. i always assumed that the working environment for employees as well as payment would generally be above average.<br /> <br /> after all the company's theoretical reason d'etre is to make things suck as much possible for as much of the world as they can.<br /> not for their comparatively fewer employees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:14:06-07:00","id":960702,"title":"","content":"Well, there are a few incentives, but the major incentive is patriotism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:27:21-07:00","id":960707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=960681#post960681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> in that case what's the incentive to become a soldier? when you could make about just as much from a blue collar job with no skill requirements? why risk your life?<br /> <br /> concerning pentex. i always assumed that the working environment for employees as well as payment would generally be above average.<br /> <br /> after all the company's theoretical reason d'etre is to make things suck as much possible for as much of the world as they can.<br /> not for their comparatively fewer employees.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is arguable if they are not better off if they make things suck for they employes as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:55:38-07:00","id":960742,"title":"","content":"Was just asking how things could suck more working at otolleys, then at Mcdonalds,Wendys, or burger king","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T17:31:13-07:00","id":960754,"title":"","content":"You're working for Pentex. So you run the risk of eating the wrong burger on lunch break on day and ending up a fomor. That's sucky enough to make an already iffy job horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T17:36:28-07:00","id":960757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=960754#post960754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're working for Pentex. So you run the risk of eating the wrong burger on lunch break on day and ending up a fomor. That's sucky enough to make an already iffy job horrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, typically, it's the risk of working in conditions as described in Upton Sinclair's The Jungle, or eating from them. This can make you susceptible to being possessed by a being you might not otherwise be as no one bothers to sort out bodies that might happen to end up on the cutting floor due to accidents in a hazardous environment, but not really the &quot;bam you're a monster now&quot; kind of thing, unless you' want to play things that way. The other risks are like those of working in a &quot;normal&quot; socially toxic environment where the shit floats to the top, and then some..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:13:02-07:00","id":960774,"title":"","content":"oh curious, how much Does a Kindred probaly need to pay a ghoul to content himself that hes &quot;Cherishing those who serve&quot; as instructed in the book of nod.<br /> <br /> Though a lot of cases, if you dont have money, most Kindred worth their salt, can find another way to make them feel cherished...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:09:04-07:00","id":960846,"title":"","content":"Well, it really depends on the standard of living that the ghoul was used to before they came into your service. If you are just picking up teenage runaway girls, who are terrified of the more dangerous human predators who will rape them until they bleed before enslaving them for profit, you could probably get away with providing them with the equivalent of V20 Resources 1. If you are ghouling a lawyer, you may need to provide V20 Resources 3, just to let them keep up appearances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:22:28-07:00","id":960855,"title":"","content":"I would tend to imagine that the Pentex board would have next to no interest in the day-to-day details of how a subordinate company were run, so as long it remained profitable or an expedient cover for questionable activities. The way Pentex would be sensibly executed, and somewhat in the direction of the way it's been written towards in V20, is a company whose subordinate-corporation day to day employees have no contact with anything directly to do with the Wyrm and whose subordinate executives are in the great majority utterly ignorant of the real purpose or significance of Pentex as an entity if they know what &quot;Pentex&quot; is at all. There's many ways to skin a cat as far as uncovering Pentex's nefarious intentions or damning criminal acts goes- between corporate rivals, supernaturals not directly interested in metaphysical questions, Glass Walker/garou assets, and government agencies with some actual interest in doing their job, the burden of Pentex's masquerade should be as formidable as that of any Kindred, if not moreso (Vampires have fantastically easy access to mind control, as far as splats go).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 08-31-2016, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:35:03-07:00","id":960911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/921583-job-paygrade-and-resources?p=960846#post960846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it really depends on the standard of living that the ghoul was used to before they came into your service. If you are just picking up teenage runaway girls, who are terrified of the more dangerous human predators who will rape them until they bleed before enslaving them for profit, you could probably get away with providing them with the equivalent of V20 Resources 1. If you are ghouling a lawyer, you may need to provide V20 Resources 3, just to let them keep up appearances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could also see it where the ghoul needs a little higher resources and other support than before, to compensate for his time being in your service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:28:08-07:00","id":961011,"title":"","content":"Yes, though it depends on the type of ghoul. If you are picking up teenage runaway girls so you can play the vampire pimp, you just have to treat them better than your competitors (above and beyond just giving them blood). I think that you could even get away with allowing them to keep 80% of their earnings (most pimps take 50% or more) in exchange for protecting them from the human predators of the street. With Dominate 3, you could keep competitors and cops away from your girls, allowing you to focus your attention on the threat that comes from the johns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:32:54-07:00","id":961168,"title":"","content":"Trying to see which kindred WOULD become that pimp..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T15:08:25-07:00","id":961261,"title":"","content":"Any Ventrue with a taste for teenage girls (or for a specific ethnicity of women) would work. Alternatively, I imagine a few Dominate Malkavians would be interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T16:37:46-07:00","id":961282,"title":"","content":"Oh whats a Vampire Pimp going to do when his Girls come under attacks during the Day? <br /> <br /> I liked the idea, holding to the letter and spirit of it, but radically deviating from the ideal of household servant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T19:02:36-07:00","id":961339,"title":"","content":"Well, smart vampires would just have them working nights (working them for the after church crowd would be tacky anyway). Otherwise, they could just have them as ghouls (Potence 1 goes a long way towards making them effective against the average john). The money is not in the brothel panel trucks or the streetwalkers, it is in the call girls ($500 a night or up). <br /> <br /> Heck, vampire pimps could get rid of a lot of competition by helping the girls who work for the other pimps off the streets (their girls will want their blood, so they will not leave). If the pimps try to retaliate, use Dominate to force them to go to the closest police station to confess their worst crimes to the police.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:42:06-07:00","id":961392,"title":"","content":"Just ghoul a bunch of pimps instead and try to establish a local monopoly on the sex trade. Why sweat the small stuff yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T22:19:17-07:00","id":961455,"title":"","content":"Well, it is about effective management. Pimps are parasites and, if you keep them as the middle men, they will just be inefficient. Anyway, you will be responsible for the sins that they commit in your name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T22:29:18-07:00","id":961460,"title":"","content":"That is an interesting angle. Would a ghoul or person you have controlled via dominate, cause YOu to make a humanity roll when he does something that ticks off the box for calling for one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:55:47-07:00","id":961631,"title":"","content":"They are nothing more than a tool at that point. If a bullet fired from a gun kills a person, is the bullet morally culpable or is the person who pulled the trigger morally culpable? And I think that both people would roll, you for your order and them for their action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T03:23:25-07:00","id":962176,"title":"","content":"Agreed, but are you culpable for things they do that you dont explicitly command, communicate a desire for through innuendo) that they do on their own initiative<br /> <br /> if a ghoul kills a troublesom hoodlum who is terrorizing his masters neighbourhood, is his master culpable?<br /> <br /> Is the Prince Culpable for Every single thing the whole court does? He should degenerate into a Wight within a week if thats the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T03:34:30-07:00","id":962179,"title":"","content":"If the domitor has engineered his ghoul's action, yes. If the prince has engineered those repugnant actions, rather than merely permitting them to be done, then yes, he is culpable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T18:33:30-07:00","id":964003,"title":"","content":"a fair point<br /> <br /> I guess a major facet is do you know about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou12